@using global::Backlog.Modules.Progress.Abstractions.DataTransferObjects
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Progress.Abstractions.Services
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Buttons
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Feedback
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Menus
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Progress
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Progress.UI.Planning
@using global::Backlog.SharedKernel.Results
@implements IDisposable
@*
    The In progress tab's two views (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md
    #following-a-sprint): Now, the host's view by task, and the sprint view of the
    series the header's repository scope works to.

    While Progress is on and the scope holds a repository of a series switched on
    with a sprint to show, the header carries the Now | Sprint n switch; otherwise
    nothing here is drawn but the host's Now view, exactly as it is without Progress
    (.devbook/domain/progress/requirements.md#a-repository-in-no-series-keeps-the-in-progress-view).
    The host draws Now and places the switch it is handed in its own header, so the
    switch never moves between the two.

    The sprint is read through ISprintProgress when the sprint view opens, on a step
    to another sprint and on Refresh, and never on its own timer — the Now view's own
    terms. The host's Revision only redraws, so the outside line takes in a read of its
    sessions and pull requests as it lands. A scope with repositories of several series
    shows the first series in scope order.

    Over the board, while the open sprint is shown and its series shows in the daily
    brief, the Since yesterday strip (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#the-daily-strip),
    written from the same reading by SprintDailyMapper.

    While the sprint shown is the open one it takes writes
    (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#filling-a-sprint): "Add to sprint…" beside
    Refresh, over the tasks the host lists (Candidates), and a menu on every row for the
    goal mark, the note and open question, and taking the task out. Each goes through
    ISprintSeriesPlanning, and the sprint is read again once it lands. A closed sprint
    draws no menu and no Add.

    Open, a SprintViewRequest from the host — the weekly brief's "Open Sprint n"
    (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#sprints-in-the-briefs) — opens the sprint view
    on that series and that sprint, whichever series the scope would pick first; OnOpened
    tells the host it was taken, so it is not taken again when the tab is drawn anew.

    A series switched on with no sprint yet carries the switch too, named for the sprint
    it will start — "Sprint 1" — and its sprint side says no sprint has started and offers
    "Start Sprint 1…" (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#starting-the-first-sprint):
    SprintStartDialog, then one StartSprintAsync. The open sprint's goal card offers
    "Edit goal" (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#writing-the-sprint-goal):
    SprintGoalDialog, then one SetSprintGoalAsync.

    "Close sprint…" sits beside them on the open sprint
    (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#closing-a-sprint): SprintCloseDialog over the
    last reading, written by SprintCloseMapper, and one CloseSprintAsync through
    ISprintSeriesPlanning. Once it lands the view opens on the sprint it started; the
    closed sprint is a step back, read-only like every closed one.

    A series saved anywhere else - pulled from another desktop by the sync, or changed
    from Settings or a task - raises ISprintSeriesPlanning.Changed: the series is found
    again and, while the sprint view is open, the sprint is read again, as Refresh does.
    What the person has open stays open with what they put in it - the Close dialog's
    choices and next goal, a note being written, the Add picker - over the fresh reading;
    the Close dialog closes only once the sprint it would close is no longer open.
*@

@if (_series is { } series && SwitchName(series) is { } sprintName)
{
    var viewSwitch = Switch(sprintName);
    if (_sprint)
    {
        <div class="in-progress-sprints" data-testid="in-progress-sprints">
            <Alert Message="@_writeError" TestId="in-progress-sprint-write-error" />
            @* The model is null while the sprint is read and when it could not be: the
               board draws its header alone then — the switch and Refresh with it — and
               the error or a spinner under it. *@
            <SprintBoard Model="_model"
                         Error="@_error"
                         Empty="@(NotStarted ? NotStartedState(series, sprintName) : null)"
                         OnEditGoal="@(Writable is null ? default : EventCallback.Factory.Create(this, OpenGoal))"
                         Outside="@OutsideWork"
                         ViewSwitch="viewSwitch"
                         OnPrevious="() => StepAsync(-1)"
                         OnNext="() => StepAsync(1)"
                         OnOpenTask="OpenTaskAsync"
                         OnOpenPullRequest="pull => OnOpenPullRequest.InvokeAsync(pull)"
                         RowMenu="@(Writable is null ? null : RowMenuFor)"
                         OnRowMenu="OnRowMenuAsync">
                <Daily>
                    @if (_daily is { } daily)
                    {
                        <SprintDailyStrip Model="daily" Table="Table" />
                    }
                </Daily>
                <Actions>
                    @if (!NotStarted)
                    {
                        if (Writable is not null && Candidates is not null)
                        {
                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Secondary"
                                       Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                       TestId="in-progress-sprint-add"
                                       OnClick="OpenPicker">Add to sprint…</AppButton>
                        }
                        if (Writable is not null)
                        {
                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Secondary"
                                       Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                       TestId="in-progress-sprint-close"
                                       Disabled="@(_model is null || _writing)"
                                       OnClick="OpenClose">Close sprint…</AppButton>
                        }
                        @* The whole sprint as a table for PowerPoint and mail
                           (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#copying-a-sprint-as-a-table):
                           every item, whatever the board's filter shows. Refused while
                           there is no sprint read to copy. *@
                        <CopyButton Text="@Table.Text"
                                    Html="@Table.Html"
                                    Label="Copy as table"
                                    Disabled="@(_model is null)"
                                    DisabledReason="The sprint is still being read"
                                    ButtonBaseClass="btn btn--ghost btn--small"
                                    StatusCssClass="copy-button__status"
                                    TestId="in-progress-sprint-copy-table"
                                    ButtonTestId="in-progress-sprint-copy-table-button"
                                    StatusTestId="in-progress-sprint-copy-table-status">Copy as table</CopyButton>
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                                   Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                   TestId="in-progress-sprint-refresh"
                                   Busy="_reading"
                                   BusyLabel="Reading"
                                   OnClick="RefreshAsync">Refresh</AppButton>
                    }
                </Actions>
            </SprintBoard>
            @if (NotStarted)
            {
                <SprintStartDialog Open="_startOpen"
                                   OpenChanged="CloseStart"
                                   SprintName="@sprintName"
                                   SeriesName="@series.Name"
                                   StartWeekday="@series.StartWeekday"
                                   DefaultStart="@SprintStartRules.DefaultStart(Today, series.StartWeekday)"
                                   Busy="_writing"
                                   Error="@_startError"
                                   OnStart="StartSprintAsync" />
            }
            @if (Writable is { } open)
            {
                <SprintGoalDialog Open="_goalOpen"
                                  OpenChanged="CloseGoal"
                                  SprintName="@open.Name"
                                  Current="@open.Goal"
                                  Busy="_writing"
                                  Error="@_goalError"
                                  OnSave="SaveGoalAsync" />
                <SprintAddPicker Open="_picking"
                                 OpenChanged="value => _picking = value"
                                 SprintName="@open.Name"
                                 Repositories="@series.Repositories"
                                 Choices="@_choices"
                                 Status="@_addStatus"
                                 Error="@_addError"
                                 Busy="_writing"
                                 OnChosen="AddAsync" />
                <SprintItemNoteDialog Open="_noteFor is not null"
                                      OpenChanged="CloseNote"
                                      TaskTitle="@(_noteFor?.Title ?? string.Empty)"
                                      SprintName="@open.Name"
                                      Current="@NoteOf(open, _noteFor)"
                                      Busy="_writing"
                                      Error="@_noteError"
                                      OnSave="SaveNoteAsync" />
                <SprintCloseDialog Open="_closing is not null"
                                   OpenChanged="CloseCloseDialog"
                                   Model="_closing"
                                   Busy="_writing"
                                   Error="@_closeError"
                                   OnClose="CloseSprintAsync" />
            }
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        @Now(viewSwitch)
    }
}
else
{
    @Now(null)
}

@code {
    [Inject] private IServiceProvider Services { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The header's repository scope, by alias, in its order; empty for every
    /// repository. The Brain's reserved empty value is no repository.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Repositories { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The Now view, given the switch to draw beside its title — null while
    /// there is no sprint to switch to, which leaves it exactly as it is.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public RenderFragment<RenderFragment?> Now { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The host's live work against tasks the sprint does not hold, asked with
    /// the ids of the tasks it does. Null draws the outside line with nothing in it.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Func<IReadOnlySet<Guid>, IReadOnlyList<SprintBoardOutside>>? Outside { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Moves whenever the host has something new to show — a read of its
    /// sessions and pull requests landing — so an open sprint view redraws its outside
    /// line.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int Revision { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A member, a Needs you card or an outside task was pressed.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Guid> OnOpenTask { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A pull request chip was pressed: its <c>owner/name#number</c> key.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnOpenPullRequest { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The sprint view opened, or Refresh was pressed: the host reads its own
    /// sessions and pull requests, as its Now view does when it opens.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<bool> OnRead { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Every task the host knows, for "Add to sprint…": the picker keeps those
    /// in the series' repositories. Unset, there is no Add; the row menu stays.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Func<IReadOnlyList<SprintCandidate>>? Candidates { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Open the sprint view on this sprint of this series. Taken once per
    /// request; a series switched off, gone, or without that sprint leaves the tab as
    /// it is.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public SprintViewRequest? Open { get; set; }

    /// <summary><see cref="Open"/> was taken: the host lets the request go.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnOpened { get; set; }

    private SprintViewRequest? _opened;

    private IAppFeatureSettings? _features;
    private ISprintSeriesPlanning? _notices;
    private bool _on;
    private string _scopeKey = "\u0000";

    private SprintSeriesDto? _series;
    private bool _sprint;
    private int? _number;
    private SprintProgressDto? _progress;
    private SprintBoardModel? _model;
    private SprintDailyModel? _daily;
    private SprintBoardModel? _tableModel;
    private SprintTable _table = EmptyTable;
    private string? _error;

    private static readonly SprintTable EmptyTable = SprintTableClipboard.Build([], []);

    /// <summary>The table Copy as table puts on the clipboard, built once per sprint
    /// read rather than on every render.</summary>
    private SprintTable Table
    {
        get
        {
            if (!ReferenceEquals(_tableModel, _model))
            {
                _tableModel = _model;
                _table = _model is null ? EmptyTable : SprintTableClipboard.Build(_model);
            }

            return _table;
        }
    }
    private bool _reading;
    private int _generation;
    private int _findGeneration;

    private bool _picking;
    private IReadOnlyList<SprintAddChoice> _choices = [];
    private string? _addStatus;
    private string? _addError;
    private bool _writing;
    private SprintMemberDto? _noteFor;
    private string? _noteError;
    private string? _writeError;
    private SprintCloseModel? _closing;
    private string? _closeError;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _features = Services.GetService(typeof(IAppFeatureSettings)) as IAppFeatureSettings;
        _on = IsOn();
        if (_features is not null) _features.Changed += OnFeaturesChanged;
        _notices = Planning;
        if (_notices is not null) _notices.Changed += OnSeriesChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// A series was saved somewhere else — most often pulled from another desktop — so
    /// the series is found again and an open sprint view reads its sprint again. The
    /// view's own writes raise this too, after they have read; the second read is the
    /// same sprint, on the roadmap band's terms.
    /// </summary>
    private void OnSeriesChanged() => _ = InvokeAsync(async () =>
    {
        if (!_on) return;

        await FindSeriesAsync();
        KeepOpenDialogs();
        StateHasChanged();
    });

    /// <summary>
    /// After an outside read, what the person has open follows the fresh reading without
    /// losing what they put in it: the Close dialog is drawn again over the sprint as it
    /// now stands — it keeps its choices and next goal while it stays open — and the Add
    /// picker offers what the series now leaves to add. When the sprint shown is no
    /// longer the open one, there is nothing left to close. A reading that failed leaves
    /// both as they were.
    /// </summary>
    private void KeepOpenDialogs()
    {
        if (_progress is null) return;

        if (_closing is not null)
        {
            _closing = Writable is not null && _series is { } series && _model is { } board
                ? SprintCloseMapper.ToModel(_progress, series, board)
                : null;
        }

        if (_picking && _series is { } current && Writable is { } open && Candidates is not null)
        {
            _choices = SprintPlanning.Choices(current, open, Candidates());
        }
    }

    private bool IsOn() => _features?.IsEnabled(ProgressFeatures.Progress) ?? false;

    private void OnFeaturesChanged() => _ = InvokeAsync(async () =>
    {
        var on = IsOn();
        if (on == _on) return;

        _on = on;
        await FindSeriesAsync();
        StateHasChanged();
    });

    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        // The count leads, so every repository ([]) and the Brain alone ([""]) differ.
        var key = $"{Repositories.Count}\u001e{string.Join("\u001f", Repositories.Select(alias => alias.Trim().ToUpperInvariant()))}";
        if (key != _scopeKey)
        {
            _scopeKey = key;
            await FindSeriesAsync();
        }

        if (Open is { } request && !ReferenceEquals(request, _opened))
        {
            _opened = request;
            await OpenSprintAsync(request);
            await OnOpened.InvokeAsync();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The sprint view on <paramref name="request"/>'s sprint, when Progress is
    /// on and its series is switched on and holds that sprint.</summary>
    private async Task OpenSprintAsync(SprintViewRequest request)
    {
        if (!_on || Planning is not { } planning) return;

        // A look for the scope's series still under way would put its own series back.
        var generation = ++_findGeneration;
        var listed = await planning.ListSeriesAsync();
        if (generation != _findGeneration || listed.IsFailure) return;

        var series = listed.Value.FirstOrDefault(candidate => candidate.Id == request.SeriesId && candidate.IsOn);
        if (series is null || series.Sprints.All(sprint => sprint.Number != request.Number)) return;

        _series = series;
        _number = request.Number;
        _sprint = true;
        Clear();

        await OnRead.InvokeAsync(false);
        await ReadSprintAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>The first series switched on, holding a scoped repository, with a
    /// sprint to show — or none, which leaves the Now view as it is.</summary>
    private async Task FindSeriesAsync()
    {
        // A scope change and a feature switch can both be looking at once; the last
        // to start is the one that counts.
        var generation = ++_findGeneration;
        var found = _on ? await SeriesInScopeAsync() : null;
        if (generation != _findGeneration) return;

        var changed = found?.Id != _series?.Id;
        _series = found;

        if (_series is null)
        {
            _sprint = false;
            Clear();
            return;
        }

        if (changed)
        {
            _number = null;
            Clear();
        }

        if (_sprint) await ReadSprintAsync();
    }

    private async Task<SprintSeriesDto?> SeriesInScopeAsync()
    {
        if (Services.GetService(typeof(ISprintSeriesPlanning)) is not ISprintSeriesPlanning planning) return null;

        var listed = await planning.ListSeriesAsync();
        if (listed.IsFailure) return null;

        // A series with no sprint yet counts too: its sprint side offers to start the
        // first. Among every repository, one that runs a sprint comes first.
        var candidates = listed.Value.Where(series => series.IsOn).ToList();
        var scope = Repositories.Select(alias => alias.Trim()).Where(alias => alias.Length > 0).ToList();

        // Every repository is in scope when none is chosen: the first series that runs.
        if (Repositories.Count == 0) return candidates.FirstOrDefault(series => series.Sprints.Count > 0) ?? candidates.FirstOrDefault();

        foreach (var alias in scope)
        {
            var series = candidates.FirstOrDefault(candidate => candidate.Repositories.Contains(alias, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase));
            if (series is not null) return series;
        }

        return null;
    }

    private void Clear()
    {
        _progress = null;
        _model = null;
        _daily = null;
        _error = null;
        _writeError = null;
        _picking = false;
        _noteFor = null;
        _closing = null;
        _closeError = null;
        _startOpen = false;
        _startError = null;
        _goalOpen = false;
        _goalError = null;
    }

    // ---- Starting the first sprint and wording the goal ---------------------------------

    private bool _startOpen;
    private string? _startError;
    private bool _goalOpen;
    private string? _goalError;

    /// <summary>The series in scope has not started its first sprint: its sprint side
    /// offers to start one rather than reading a sprint.</summary>
    private bool NotStarted => _series is { Sprints.Count: 0 };

    /// <summary>Today by the module's clock, which the Start dialog counts its default
    /// day from.</summary>
    private DateOnly Today =>
        DateOnly.FromDateTime(((Services.GetService(typeof(TimeProvider)) as TimeProvider) ?? TimeProvider.System).GetLocalNow().DateTime);

    private RenderFragment NotStartedState(SprintSeriesDto series, string sprintName) =>
        @<EmptyState Title="No sprint has started yet"
                     Description="@NotStartedLine(series)"
                     TestId="in-progress-sprint-not-started">
            <Action>
                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Primary"
                           TestId="in-progress-sprint-start"
                           OnClick="OpenStart">Start @sprintName…</AppButton>
            </Action>
        </EmptyState>;

    private static string NotStartedLine(SprintSeriesDto series) =>
        $"{series.Name} runs {(series.Length == SprintLength.OneWeek ? "one-week" : "two-week")} sprints from a {series.StartWeekday}. Start the first to plan into it.";

    private void OpenStart()
    {
        _startError = null;
        _startOpen = true;
    }

    private void CloseStart(bool open)
    {
        if (open || _writing) return;
        _startOpen = false;
        _startError = null;
    }

    /// <summary>Starts the series' first sprint through the module and opens the view on
    /// it. A refusal stays in the dialog in the module's words.</summary>
    private async Task StartSprintAsync(SprintStart start)
    {
        if (_series is not { } series || !NotStarted || Planning is not { } planning || _writing) return;

        _number = null;
        Result<SprintSeriesDto> started;
        try
        {
            started = await WriteAsync(() => planning.StartSprintAsync(series.Id, start.On, start.Goal));
        }
        catch (Exception exception) when (exception is IOException or System.Data.Common.DbException or UnauthorizedAccessException)
        {
            _startError = $"The sprint could not be started: {exception.Message}";
            return;
        }

        if (started.IsFailure)
        {
            _startError = started.Error.Message;
            return;
        }

        _startError = null;
        _startOpen = false;
    }

    private void OpenGoal()
    {
        if (Writable is null) return;
        _goalError = null;
        _goalOpen = true;
    }

    private void CloseGoal(bool open)
    {
        if (open || _writing) return;
        _goalOpen = false;
        _goalError = null;
    }

    /// <summary>Writes the open sprint's goal through the module; the goal card shows it
    /// once the sprint is read again. A refusal stays in the dialog.</summary>
    private async Task SaveGoalAsync(string goal)
    {
        if (_series is not { } series || Writable is not { } open || Planning is not { } planning || _writing) return;

        if (string.Equals(goal, open.Goal ?? string.Empty, StringComparison.Ordinal))
        {
            _goalOpen = false;
            return;
        }

        Result<SprintSeriesDto> written;
        try
        {
            written = await WriteAsync(() => planning.SetSprintGoalAsync(series.Id, open.Number, goal));
        }
        catch (Exception exception) when (exception is IOException or System.Data.Common.DbException or UnauthorizedAccessException)
        {
            _goalError = $"The goal could not be saved: {exception.Message}";
            return;
        }

        if (written.IsFailure)
        {
            _goalError = written.Error.Message;
            return;
        }

        _goalError = null;
        _goalOpen = false;
    }

    // ---- Planning the open sprint -------------------------------------------------------

    /// <summary>The sprint shown, when it is the series' open sprint — the one sprint that
    /// takes writes — else null.</summary>
    private SprintDto? Writable =>
        _series?.OpenSprint is { } open && _progress is { IsOpen: true } shown && shown.Number == open.Number ? open : null;

    private IReadOnlyList<MenuItem> RowMenuFor(SprintBoardRow row) =>
        Writable is { } open && MemberOf(row) is { } member ? SprintPlanning.RowMenu(open, member) : [];

    private SprintMemberDto? MemberOf(SprintBoardRow row) =>
        Guid.TryParse(row.TaskId, out var id) ? _progress?.Members.FirstOrDefault(member => member.TaskId == id) : null;

    private static SprintItemNote NoteOf(SprintDto sprint, SprintMemberDto? member)
    {
        var item = member is null ? null : SprintPlanning.ItemOf(sprint, member.TaskId);
        return new SprintItemNote(item?.Note, item?.OpenQuestion ?? false);
    }

    private void CloseNote(bool open)
    {
        if (!open) _noteFor = null;
    }

    private void OpenPicker()
    {
        if (_series is not { } series || Writable is not { } open || Candidates is null) return;

        _choices = SprintPlanning.Choices(series, open, Candidates());
        _addStatus = null;
        _addError = null;
        _picking = true;
    }

    private async Task AddAsync(SprintAddChoice choice)
    {
        if (_series is not { } series || Writable is not { } open || Planning is not { } planning || _writing) return;

        Result<SprintSeriesDto>? written = null;
        if (choice.Kind == SprintAddKind.Plan)
        {
            written = await WriteAsync(() => planning.LinkPlanAsync(series.Id, open.Number, choice.Id));
        }
        else if (Guid.TryParse(choice.Id, out var taskId))
        {
            written = await WriteAsync(() => planning.AddTaskAsync(series.Id, open.Number, taskId));
        }

        if (written is null) return;
        if (written.IsFailure)
        {
            _addError = written.Error.Message;
            return;
        }

        _addError = null;
        _addStatus = choice.Kind == SprintAddKind.Plan ? $"Linked {choice.Label}." : $"Added “{choice.Label}”.";
        if (_series is { } updated && updated.OpenSprint is { } still && Candidates is not null)
        {
            _choices = SprintPlanning.Choices(updated, still, Candidates());
        }
    }

    private async Task OnRowMenuAsync(SprintRowMenuChoice choice)
    {
        if (_series is not { } series || Writable is not { } open || MemberOf(choice.Row) is not { } member) return;
        if (Planning is not { } planning || _writing) return;

        if (choice.Item.Id == SprintPlanning.EditNote)
        {
            _noteError = null;
            _noteFor = member;
            return;
        }

        var id = member.TaskId;
        Func<Task<Result<SprintSeriesDto>>>? write = choice.Item.Id switch
        {
            SprintPlanning.MarkGoal => () => planning.MarkGoalAsync(series.Id, open.Number, id, true),
            SprintPlanning.UnmarkGoal => () => planning.MarkGoalAsync(series.Id, open.Number, id, false),
            SprintPlanning.MarkQuestion => () => planning.SetOpenQuestionAsync(series.Id, open.Number, id, true),
            SprintPlanning.ClearQuestion => () => planning.SetOpenQuestionAsync(series.Id, open.Number, id, false),
            SprintPlanning.RemoveTask => () => planning.RemoveTaskAsync(series.Id, open.Number, id),
            SprintPlanning.UnlinkPlan when member.PlanTag is { } plan => () => planning.UnlinkPlanAsync(series.Id, open.Number, plan),
            _ => null
        };
        if (write is null) return;

        var written = await WriteAsync(write);
        _writeError = written.IsFailure ? written.Error.Message : null;
    }

    private async Task SaveNoteAsync(SprintItemNote note)
    {
        if (_series is not { } series || Writable is not { } open || _noteFor is not { } member || Planning is not { } planning) return;

        var current = NoteOf(open, member);
        var id = member.TaskId;
        var number = open.Number;

        if (!string.Equals(current.Note, note.Note, StringComparison.Ordinal))
        {
            var noted = await WriteAsync(() => planning.SetNoteAsync(series.Id, number, id, note.Note));
            if (noted.IsFailure)
            {
                _noteError = noted.Error.Message;
                return;
            }
        }

        if (current.OpenQuestion != note.OpenQuestion)
        {
            var asked = await WriteAsync(() => planning.SetOpenQuestionAsync(series.Id, number, id, note.OpenQuestion));
            if (asked.IsFailure)
            {
                _noteError = asked.Error.Message;
                return;
            }
        }

        _noteError = null;
        _noteFor = null;
    }

    // ---- Closing the open sprint --------------------------------------------------------

    /// <summary>Opens the Close dialog on the sprint as last read: its unfinished items
    /// are the members the board shows as not done, which is the module's own reading.</summary>
    private void OpenClose()
    {
        if (_series is not { } series || Writable is null || _progress is not { } progress || _model is not { } board) return;

        _closeError = null;
        _closing = SprintCloseMapper.ToModel(progress, series, board);
    }

    private void CloseCloseDialog(bool open)
    {
        if (!open) _closing = null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Closes the open sprint and starts the next one through the module
    /// (<c>.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#closing-a-sprint</c>), then opens the view
    /// on the sprint it started; the closed one stays a step back. A refusal stays in the
    /// dialog in the module's words, over a fresh reading: when an item turned unfinished
    /// since the dialog opened, it is listed now, on Carry, beside the choices already
    /// made.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task CloseSprintAsync(SprintCloseDecision decision)
    {
        if (_series is not { } series || Writable is null || Planning is not { } planning || _writing) return;

        // The read after the close opens on the open sprint, which is then the new one.
        var shown = _number;
        _number = null;
        var closed = await WriteAsync(() => planning.CloseSprintAsync(series.Id, SprintCloseMapper.Outcomes(decision), decision.NextGoal));
        if (closed.IsFailure)
        {
            _number = shown;
            _closeError = closed.Error.Message;
            await ReadSprintAsync();
            if (_closing is not null && _series is { } still && _progress is { IsOpen: true } progress && _model is { } board)
            {
                _closing = SprintCloseMapper.ToModel(progress, still, board);
            }

            return;
        }

        _closeError = null;
        _closing = null;
    }

    private ISprintSeriesPlanning? Planning => Services.GetService(typeof(ISprintSeriesPlanning)) as ISprintSeriesPlanning;

    /// <summary>One write through the module: the series it answers with replaces the
    /// one held, and the sprint is read again so the board shows what changed — unless
    /// the scope moved to another series while it was written, which then stays.</summary>
    private async Task<Result<SprintSeriesDto>> WriteAsync(Func<Task<Result<SprintSeriesDto>>> write)
    {
        _writing = true;
        try
        {
            var written = await write();
            if (written.IsSuccess && written.Value.Id == _series?.Id)
            {
                _series = written.Value;
                await ReadSprintAsync();
            }

            return written;
        }
        finally
        {
            _writing = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>What the switch calls the sprint view: the sprint it opens on — the
    /// open one, or the last one the series ran.</summary>
    private string? SwitchName(SprintSeriesDto series)
    {
        if (series.Sprints.Count == 0) return SprintSeriesCardModel.NextName(series.NamePattern, 1) ?? "Sprint 1";

        var sprint = _number is { } number
            ? series.Sprints.FirstOrDefault(candidate => candidate.Number == number)
            : series.OpenSprint ?? series.Sprints.LastOrDefault();

        return (sprint ?? series.OpenSprint ?? series.Sprints.LastOrDefault())?.Name;
    }

    private RenderFragment Switch(string sprintName) => @<SprintViewSwitch Sprint="_sprint"
                                                                            SprintName="@sprintName"
                                                                            SprintChanged="OnSwitchAsync" />;

    private async Task OnSwitchAsync(bool sprint)
    {
        _sprint = sprint;
        if (!sprint)
        {
            // Back on Now, the switch names the open sprint again and opens on it.
            _number = null;
            Clear();
            return;
        }

        await OnRead.InvokeAsync(false);
        await ReadSprintAsync();
    }

    private async Task StepAsync(int step)
    {
        if (_series is null || _progress is null) return;

        var numbers = _series.Sprints.Select(sprint => sprint.Number).OrderBy(number => number).ToList();
        int? next = step < 0
            ? numbers.LastOrDefault(number => number < _progress.Number) is var previous and > 0 ? previous : null
            : numbers.FirstOrDefault(number => number > _progress.Number) is var later and > 0 ? later : null;
        if (next is null) return;

        _number = next;
        await ReadSprintAsync();
    }

    private async Task RefreshAsync()
    {
        await OnRead.InvokeAsync(true);
        await ReadSprintAsync();
    }

    private async Task ReadSprintAsync()
    {
        if (_series is not { } series) return;
        if (series.Sprints.Count == 0)
        {
            // Nothing to read before the first sprint: the side offers to start one.
            _generation++;
            _progress = null;
            _model = null;
            _daily = null;
            _error = null;
            _reading = false;
            return;
        }
        if (Services.GetService(typeof(ISprintProgress)) is not ISprintProgress progress)
        {
            _progress = null;
            _model = null;
            _daily = null;
            _error = "The sprint could not be read: Progress is not composed in this host.";
            return;
        }

        var generation = ++_generation;
        _reading = true;
        try
        {
            var read = await progress.ReadAsync(series.Id, _number);
            if (generation != _generation) return;

            if (read.IsFailure)
            {
                _progress = null;
                _model = null;
                _daily = null;
                _error = read.Error.Message;
                return;
            }

            _progress = read.Value;
            _model = SprintBoardMapper.ToModel(read.Value, series);
            _daily = SprintDailyMapper.ToModel(read.Value, series);
            _error = null;
        }
        finally
        {
            if (generation == _generation) _reading = false;
        }
    }

    private IReadOnlyList<SprintBoardOutside> OutsideWork =>
        Outside is null || _progress is null
            ? []
            : Outside(_progress.Members.Select(member => member.TaskId).ToHashSet());

    private Task OpenTaskAsync(string taskId) =>
        Guid.TryParse(taskId, out var id) ? OnOpenTask.InvokeAsync(id) : Task.CompletedTask;

    public void Dispose()
    {
        if (_features is not null) _features.Changed -= OnFeaturesChanged;
        if (_notices is not null) _notices.Changed -= OnSeriesChanged;
    }
}
